This project does not redistribute WaterFurnace firmware or any proprietary code.
The documentation in docs/ describes the device's local interface (register map,
CGI protocol, fault codes) as recovered by reverse-engineering for the purpose of
interoperability with hardware the user owns, and records diagnostic findings from
a specific unit.

Any procedure that modifies device firmware (see docs/local-access.md) is provided
for repair of hardware you own and is performed entirely at your own risk. It may
carry legal implications depending on your jurisdiction. Nothing here is legal
